wait for no cart face while an eject has the shelf hidden

The first frame after a game also waited 66.2 ms for the shelf's cart faces
(traced on the handheld, 2026-10-31, see next-eject-ground-on-a-thread).
0016 frees all but the seated cart's face while a game plays, so ejecting
asks for the drawn span again, marked on screen, and CartFaces::sync blocks
the frame until it is built.

But on a framed panel an eject draws none of the shelf until the screen
has powered off over the game: that arm of App::draw is draw_powering, a
black rect and the game. face_wants now marks nothing on screen while that
is so (App::shelf_hidden, mirroring the arm), so the faces are built in that
time and waited for only once the shelf is drawn -- no frame shows a cart
without the art it had before.

A new test ejects from a game on a 752x560 panel and checks, frame by
frame, that no face is waited for while the draw list is draw_powering's,
and that the faces are waited for again once the shelf is drawn. It fails
without the change. Not yet run on the handheld.

Applies on top of 0037, upstream 91499a9.

